<article class="env-definition" id="03SM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03SM">Definition <span data-tag="03SM">33.36.1</span>.</a> Let $p$ be a prime number. Let $X$ be a scheme in characteristic $p$. The <em>absolute frobenius of $X$</em> is the morphism $F_ X : X \to X$ given by the identity on the underlying topological space and with $F_ X^\sharp : \mathcal{O}_ X \to \mathcal{O}_ X$ given by $g \mapsto g^ p$. </p>
</article>